15
00:01:53,927 --> 00:01:55,387
[♪ music increases in tempo]

16
00:01:57,389 --> 00:01:58,557
FINAL EPISODE

17
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,183
Did he go to my exhibition hall?

18
00:02:00,267 --> 00:02:01,518
[♪ music swells]

19
00:02:03,979 --> 00:02:05,522
[♪ music slows]

20
00:02:05,605 --> 00:02:07,441
[♪ music increases in tempo]

21
00:02:07,524 --> 00:02:09,359
-[grunts, exclaims]
-[grunts]

22
00:02:10,735 --> 00:02:11,945
-[Isoo grunts]
-[heavy thud]

23
00:02:14,614 --> 00:02:15,782
[panting]

24
00:02:16,283 --> 00:02:17,325
[groans]

25
00:02:18,994 --> 00:02:20,579
-[blunt thud]
-[high-pitched ringing]

26
00:02:20,662 --> 00:02:21,705
[thuds]

27
00:02:23,749 --> 00:02:24,875
[high-pitched ringing fades]

28
00:02:27,669 --> 00:02:28,670
[distorted thud]

29
00:02:32,591 --> 00:02:34,050
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

30
00:02:43,977 --> 00:02:45,312
[line ringing]

31
00:02:50,192 --> 00:02:52,194
-[fire roaring]
-[cell phone vibrating]

32
00:03:05,415 --> 00:03:06,666
[tires screech]

33
00:03:09,461 --> 00:03:10,837
How did it go?

34
00:03:10,921 --> 00:03:12,923
-There's a fire inside.
-What?

35
00:03:17,135 --> 00:03:19,304
Isoo! Jin Isoo!

36
00:03:20,764 --> 00:03:22,015
Jin Isoo!

37
00:03:23,141 --> 00:03:24,684
[♪ music increases in tempo]

38
00:03:24,768 --> 00:03:26,186
[grunts]

39
00:03:26,645 --> 00:03:27,771
[all exclaim]

40
00:03:29,856 --> 00:03:30,857
Jin Isoo!

41
00:03:32,359 --> 00:03:33,777
Jin Isoo!

42
00:03:34,444 --> 00:03:35,445
Isoo!

43
00:03:36,196 --> 00:03:37,989
Isoo! Jin Isoo!

44
00:03:38,573 --> 00:03:39,574
Jin Isoo!

45
00:03:40,116 --> 00:03:42,035
Jin Isoo!

46
00:03:42,827 --> 00:03:44,788
Get him on my back! [grunts]

47
00:03:45,539 --> 00:03:47,332
Jin Isoo! Get on my back!

48
00:03:47,415 --> 00:03:49,000
[Changun grunting]

49
00:03:50,377 --> 00:03:51,711
Call an ambulance!

50
00:03:51,795 --> 00:03:52,921
[♪ music resumes tempo]

51
00:03:53,004 --> 00:03:54,005
[Changun grunts]

52
00:03:55,090 --> 00:03:56,258
[panting] Jin Isoo.

53
00:03:56,883 --> 00:03:58,009
Can you hear me?

54
00:03:58,093 --> 00:03:59,344
[sirens approaching]

55
00:03:59,427 --> 00:04:01,513
The ambulance is on its way.
Hang in there.

56
00:04:01,596 --> 00:04:02,764
[sirens blaring]

57
00:04:04,849 --> 00:04:05,892
[tires screech]

58
00:04:08,186 --> 00:04:10,230
[Changun] Here. He's here.

59
00:04:10,313 --> 00:04:11,481
Over here!

60
00:04:11,565 --> 00:04:13,608
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

61
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:20,073
Detective Jin found all the evidence.

62
00:04:20,156 --> 00:04:21,199
Evidence?

63
00:04:22,158 --> 00:04:23,159
What evidence?

64
00:04:25,996 --> 00:04:28,874
The victims' belongings and photos.

65
00:04:29,791 --> 00:04:31,042
You have them all on display.

66
00:04:31,126 --> 00:04:32,127
Ah.

67
00:04:33,211 --> 00:04:34,212
Really?

68
00:04:35,672 --> 00:04:37,799
I wonder what he thought of it.

69
00:04:43,263 --> 00:04:44,848
[cell phone vibrating]

70
00:04:44,931 --> 00:04:46,308
[♪ music fades]

71
00:04:46,391 --> 00:04:48,268
CHIEF PARK CHANGUN

72
00:04:51,396 --> 00:04:53,607
-You should get that.
-[cell phone continues vibrating]

73
00:04:54,274 --> 00:04:55,609
It seems urgent.

74
00:04:59,195 --> 00:05:00,196
[panting] Detective Joo!

75
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,115
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

76
00:05:07,871 --> 00:05:08,872
[door slams]

77
00:05:10,624 --> 00:05:11,666
[breathes deeply]

78
00:05:12,876 --> 00:05:14,628
There's a basement inside my studio.

79
00:05:15,378 --> 00:05:18,006
Tell your boyfriend to burn it down.

80
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:20,091
I might have a visitor.

81
00:05:20,175 --> 00:05:21,593
[♪ music increases in tempo]

82
00:05:24,679 --> 00:05:26,389
[♪ music swells, fades]

83
00:05:27,307 --> 00:05:28,558
[Hyera panting] Chief.

84
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:30,268
What about Isoo?

85
00:05:30,352 --> 00:05:31,436
Ah, well...

86
00:05:31,519 --> 00:05:33,730
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

87
00:05:33,813 --> 00:05:35,023
He's in surgery right now.

88
00:05:35,565 --> 00:05:36,608
He has a brain hemorrhage.

89
00:05:36,691 --> 00:05:37,817
[sighs heavily]

90
00:05:40,612 --> 00:05:41,696
[Hyera sighs softly]

91
00:05:43,448 --> 00:05:44,449
What do we do?

92
00:05:45,033 --> 00:05:46,284
Don't worry too much.

93
00:05:46,368 --> 00:05:48,036
They said they can stop the bleeding.

94
00:05:48,119 --> 00:05:50,830
Detective Jin is going to be okay.

95
00:05:51,498 --> 00:05:52,999
What exactly happened?

96
00:05:53,083 --> 00:05:56,002
When we got there, Isoo was unconscious,

97
00:05:56,544 --> 00:05:57,879
and the basement was on fire.

98
00:05:57,963 --> 00:06:00,924
-[exhales softly]
-You mean someone set the place on fire?

99
00:06:01,007 --> 00:06:02,425
Yes.

100
00:06:02,509 --> 00:06:04,552
That person must have attacked Isoo.

101
00:06:05,345 --> 00:06:08,348
We're searching through
all the nearby security footage...

102
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,559
but the basement was destroyed.

103
00:06:12,310 --> 00:06:13,561
We won't find any evidence.

104
00:06:14,229 --> 00:06:15,271
[sighs softly]

105
00:06:16,773 --> 00:06:18,525
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[sighs heavily]

106
00:06:20,819 --> 00:06:21,903
Yes, how did it go?

107
00:06:23,113 --> 00:06:24,698
Then widen the search area.

108
00:06:25,699 --> 00:06:28,618
[angrily] Get a list of all the vehicles
spotted near the studio!

109
00:06:29,285 --> 00:06:30,370
[Kyungjin sighs softly]

110
00:06:32,288 --> 00:06:34,374
Yu Seongwon, that son of a bitch.

111
00:06:36,751 --> 00:06:38,461
[voice shaking] I should've gone with him.

112
00:06:40,005 --> 00:06:41,256
[sighs regretfully]

113
00:06:43,508 --> 00:06:45,677
-[Hyera sighs]
-[sighs heavily]

114
00:06:49,014 --> 00:06:51,516
The police chief said you are free to go.

115
00:06:54,144 --> 00:06:56,396
SURGERY STATUS
JIN ISOO, 32Y/O MALE, IN SURGERY

116
00:06:59,524 --> 00:07:00,608
[♪ music fades]

117
00:07:03,486 --> 00:07:04,904
Bro!

118
00:07:04,988 --> 00:07:07,365
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

119
00:07:08,032 --> 00:07:09,033
How did it go?

120
00:07:09,117 --> 00:07:10,660
The surgery went well.

121
00:07:10,744 --> 00:07:14,581
But on top of the trauma to his brain,
he suffered carbon monoxide poisoning,

122
00:07:14,664 --> 00:07:18,084
so it's difficult to say
when he will regain consciousness.

123
00:07:20,044 --> 00:07:21,629
Right, we'll move him to his room.

124
00:07:42,859 --> 00:07:44,694
We'll look into the suspect's vehicle.

125
00:07:45,862 --> 00:07:46,946
Mmm.

126
00:08:05,006 --> 00:08:06,007
Jin Isoo.

127
00:08:09,302 --> 00:08:10,386
You'll wake up, right?

128
00:08:15,850 --> 00:08:18,019
I know you won't let this break you.

129
00:08:25,151 --> 00:08:26,152
I'll be waiting.

130
00:08:27,737 --> 00:08:29,197
Sleep for a bit, then come back.

131
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,490
[♪ music swells]

132
00:08:31,449 --> 00:08:32,492
[♪ music fades]

133
00:08:32,575 --> 00:08:33,993
[cell phone vibrating]

134
00:08:40,792 --> 00:08:42,252
Jin Isoo is still alive.

135
00:08:42,335 --> 00:08:44,254
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

136
00:08:45,171 --> 00:08:46,172
[line disconnects]

137
00:08:49,717 --> 00:08:51,219
[monitor beeping steadily]

138
00:08:52,762 --> 00:08:54,305
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

139
00:08:57,684 --> 00:08:58,768
Chairman Choi.

140
00:09:04,023 --> 00:09:05,233
[breath trembles]

141
00:09:10,822 --> 00:09:12,448
Detective Joo Hyera.

142
00:09:13,783 --> 00:09:14,784
I'm sorry.

143
00:09:15,493 --> 00:09:16,578
Please leave.

144
00:09:19,289 --> 00:09:21,124
I will stay here.

145
00:09:41,186 --> 00:09:42,228
[door closes]

146
00:10:01,414 --> 00:10:02,498
[♪ music fades]

147
00:10:02,582 --> 00:10:06,419
NUMBER 1 SAFETY!! NUMBER 1 PUBLIC ORDER!!
GANGHA POLICE STATION

148
00:10:08,087 --> 00:10:09,130
[sighs softly]

149
00:10:11,299 --> 00:10:12,342
[scoffs softly]

150
00:10:12,425 --> 00:10:14,385
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

151
00:10:20,308 --> 00:10:22,018
[♪ music increases in tempo]

152
00:10:31,986 --> 00:10:32,987
[exhales softly]

153
00:11:14,362 --> 00:11:16,030
Should I just disappear?

154
00:11:17,615 --> 00:11:18,658
[scoffs softly]

155
00:11:19,701 --> 00:11:22,370
Should I make one final piece?

156
00:11:29,794 --> 00:11:30,878
[♪ music fades]

157
00:11:30,962 --> 00:11:32,588
[monitor beeping steadily]

158
00:11:33,464 --> 00:11:35,425
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

159
00:11:52,358 --> 00:11:53,359
[grunts softly]

160
00:12:01,451 --> 00:12:02,577
Is he awake?

161
00:12:02,660 --> 00:12:03,703
[sighs heavily]

162
00:12:08,499 --> 00:12:09,500
No.

163
00:12:12,295 --> 00:12:13,296
Go on in.

164
00:12:14,088 --> 00:12:15,923
I'll go talk to his doctor.

165
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:21,929
GANGHA JUNGANG HOSPITAL
VIP WING

166
00:12:29,270 --> 00:12:30,855
[monitor beeping steadily]

167
00:12:36,569 --> 00:12:37,904
[cell phone vibrating]

168
00:12:44,577 --> 00:12:45,787
Hello?

169
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:47,455
[Kyungjin] <i>Is Isoo awake?</i>

170
00:12:47,538 --> 00:12:48,915
He's still the same.

171
00:12:51,167 --> 00:12:52,460
Did you find anything?

172
00:12:52,543 --> 00:12:54,629
We found a vehicle
that could be the suspect's,

173
00:12:54,712 --> 00:12:55,963
but the plate is fake.

174
00:12:56,547 --> 00:12:58,174
We'll keep looking.

175
00:13:06,057 --> 00:13:07,100
[♪ music fades]

176
00:13:07,183 --> 00:13:08,393
[Kyungjin sighs softly]

177
00:13:09,477 --> 00:13:10,770
[Junyoung exhales softly]

178
00:13:12,105 --> 00:13:13,147
[pats back]

179
00:13:13,231 --> 00:13:15,525
Get it together.
We need to catch that bastard.

180
00:13:15,608 --> 00:13:17,485
[sighs deeply] Okay.

181
00:13:18,027 --> 00:13:20,696
[sighs heavily]
I don't know about Yu Seongwon,

182
00:13:20,780 --> 00:13:22,990
but if Jeong Taeseon ordered
someone to do it,

183
00:13:24,075 --> 00:13:25,326
it's probably him.

184
00:13:25,410 --> 00:13:27,078
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

185
00:13:27,161 --> 00:13:29,664
But he went off the grid
after killing Cho Pilgu.

186
00:13:29,747 --> 00:13:30,998
We don't even know his name.

187
00:13:31,082 --> 00:13:32,125
[sighs thoughtfully]

188
00:13:32,708 --> 00:13:35,503
Is there any way to track the car
after it left the studio?

189
00:13:35,586 --> 00:13:37,880
I checked all the traffic cameras,
but it disappeared.

190
00:13:39,590 --> 00:13:42,051
Did the suspect ditch the car somewhere?

191
00:13:43,469 --> 00:13:45,930
Let's search the area again
from where it disappeared.

192
00:13:48,599 --> 00:13:51,269
Mmm, the car disappeared around here.

193
00:13:51,352 --> 00:13:53,020
-Let's go.
-[cell phone vibrating]

194
00:13:54,564 --> 00:13:55,940
INCOMING CALL
NO CALLER ID

195
00:14:02,989 --> 00:14:04,824
Yes, this is Park Junyoung.

196
00:14:05,491 --> 00:14:06,659
[unknown caller] <i>Ah.</i>

197
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:10,037
We are Detective Jin Isoo's... [mouthing]

198
00:14:12,331 --> 00:14:13,583
His secret agents.

199
00:14:13,666 --> 00:14:14,876
What?

200
00:14:14,959 --> 00:14:18,004
<i>We saw on the news</i>
<i>that Detective Jin was in an accident.</i>

201
00:14:18,838 --> 00:14:19,839
So?

202
00:14:20,464 --> 00:14:24,051
He asked us to find someone for him.

203
00:14:24,635 --> 00:14:26,345
[whispering] A guy who killed a suspect.

204
00:14:26,429 --> 00:14:27,471
Did you find him?

205
00:14:27,555 --> 00:14:29,015
[secret agent] <i>We found him.</i>

206
00:14:29,098 --> 00:14:30,224
How?

207
00:14:30,308 --> 00:14:31,309
Ah.

208
00:14:31,392 --> 00:14:32,518
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

209
00:14:32,602 --> 00:14:34,145
That will remain a secret.

210
00:14:34,770 --> 00:14:36,272
His name is Han Jonghyeon.

211
00:14:36,355 --> 00:14:38,024
Date of birth is November 19, 1983.

212
00:14:40,776 --> 00:14:43,154
IDENTITY SEARCH

213
00:14:48,618 --> 00:14:49,744
NAME HAN JONGHYEON

214
00:14:50,953 --> 00:14:53,039
[secret agent] <i>His recent location</i>
<i>is Wonmok-dong.</i>

215
00:14:53,122 --> 00:14:56,000
It seems he's at a hotel
called East Hill Hotel.

216
00:14:56,083 --> 00:14:57,084
Thank you.

217
00:14:57,877 --> 00:14:59,003
-Let's go.
-Okay.

218
00:15:02,048 --> 00:15:03,090
[♪ music fades]

219
00:15:05,843 --> 00:15:06,886
[cell phone vibrating]

220
00:15:10,890 --> 00:15:11,891
Hello?

221
00:15:11,974 --> 00:15:13,601
[Taeseon] No matter how I look at it...

222
00:15:13,684 --> 00:15:14,936
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

223
00:15:15,019 --> 00:15:16,896
...to cover all this up,

224
00:15:19,357 --> 00:15:21,734
I think Seongwon
will have to commit suicide.

225
00:15:23,945 --> 00:15:26,447
<i>A mentally unstable artist</i>

226
00:15:26,530 --> 00:15:28,532
takes his life
after his studio burns down.

227
00:15:30,117 --> 00:15:31,827
The murder cases are closed unsolved.

228
00:15:31,911 --> 00:15:34,330
[♪ ominous chord swells, fades]

229
00:15:36,999 --> 00:15:38,918
And I'll become a poor mother

230
00:15:40,503 --> 00:15:42,755
who lost her child.

231
00:15:43,422 --> 00:15:44,423
Yes, understood.

232
00:15:45,299 --> 00:15:47,009
<i>Do you still have what I gave you?</i>

233
00:15:48,135 --> 00:15:50,054
He's not easy to deal with.

234
00:15:50,137 --> 00:15:51,555
[♪ music increases in tempo]

235
00:15:51,639 --> 00:15:53,641
There's no telling what he'll do.
Be careful.

236
00:15:54,767 --> 00:15:55,935
<i>When it's done,</i>

237
00:15:56,811 --> 00:15:58,104
<i>leave the country.</i>

238
00:15:58,187 --> 00:16:00,064
I'll come find you.

239
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:02,817
<i>I'm always grateful to you.</i>

240
00:16:04,318 --> 00:16:06,487
You know you're the only one
I can trust, right?

241
00:16:09,073 --> 00:16:10,199
Yes. Please don't worry.

242
00:16:10,283 --> 00:16:11,659
[♪ music swells]

243
00:16:20,584 --> 00:16:21,585
[♪ music fades]

244
00:16:25,965 --> 00:16:26,966
It's this place.

245
00:16:27,049 --> 00:16:28,426
EAST HILL HOTEL

246
00:16:28,509 --> 00:16:30,136
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

247
00:16:32,179 --> 00:16:33,180
That's Han Jonghyeon.

248
00:16:36,267 --> 00:16:37,268
You're right.

249
00:16:37,351 --> 00:16:38,561
[♪ music increases in tempo]

250
00:16:50,364 --> 00:16:51,615
[♪ music swells]

251
00:16:58,622 --> 00:16:59,707
[♪ music fades]

252
00:17:01,250 --> 00:17:02,877
-[cell phone vibrating]
-[exhales sharply]

253
00:17:04,670 --> 00:17:06,672
JEONG TAESEON

254
00:17:10,885 --> 00:17:12,053
[sighs softly]

255
00:17:14,805 --> 00:17:17,600
[Taeseon] <i>I sent you a car.</i>
<i>Come to the villa.</i>

256
00:17:17,683 --> 00:17:19,518
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

257
00:17:27,902 --> 00:17:28,903
Should we get him now?

258
00:17:29,403 --> 00:17:30,404
No.

259
00:17:30,988 --> 00:17:32,406
Let's wait and see.

260
00:17:32,490 --> 00:17:33,532
[exhales softly]

261
00:17:40,915 --> 00:17:43,167
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

262
00:17:47,088 --> 00:17:48,964
-[sighs softly]
-Please get in.

263
00:17:50,508 --> 00:17:52,259
The chairwoman sent me to escort you.

264
00:17:56,055 --> 00:17:57,181
[inhales sharply]

265
00:18:29,714 --> 00:18:30,965
[cell phone vibrating]

266
00:18:34,552 --> 00:18:37,012
Detective Joo, we found the suspect
who killed Cho Pilgu.

267
00:18:37,096 --> 00:18:39,890
Han Jonghyeon used to be
Jeong Taeseon's chief secretary.

268
00:18:39,974 --> 00:18:41,892
<i>He's on the move with Yu Seongwon.</i>

269
00:18:41,976 --> 00:18:42,977
We're following them.

270
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:45,271
Where are you? I'll be right there.

271
00:18:45,354 --> 00:18:47,398
Near Haseong. We'll keep you updated.

272
00:18:49,024 --> 00:18:50,359
[♪ music swells]

273
00:18:56,699 --> 00:18:57,825
[♪ music fades]

274
00:18:57,908 --> 00:18:59,076
[Seongwon sighs softly]

275
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:01,454
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

276
00:19:01,537 --> 00:19:02,621
Where are we going?

277
00:19:03,289 --> 00:19:05,082
This isn't the way to the villa.

278
00:19:16,093 --> 00:19:17,970
[sighs deeply]

279
00:19:23,642 --> 00:19:25,478
Did my mom tell you to kill me?

280
00:19:29,648 --> 00:19:33,527
Did she tell you
to lock me up in a psych ward again?

281
00:19:33,611 --> 00:19:35,488
[breathes deeply]

282
00:19:40,242 --> 00:19:42,453
That's what you get for pushing your luck.

283
00:19:44,163 --> 00:19:46,081
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

284
00:19:58,385 --> 00:19:59,470
[Seongwon exhales heavily]

285
00:20:01,889 --> 00:20:03,474
[♪ music increases in tempo]

286
00:20:04,642 --> 00:20:05,684
[scoffing softly]

287
00:20:08,062 --> 00:20:10,189
[♪ music turns ominous]

288
00:20:13,484 --> 00:20:15,110
-[distant gunshot]
-What was that?

289
00:20:15,861 --> 00:20:17,029
[engine revving]

290
00:20:17,112 --> 00:20:18,239
[♪ music swells]

291
00:20:19,824 --> 00:20:22,076
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

292
00:20:22,159 --> 00:20:23,452
[tires screech]

293
00:20:28,666 --> 00:20:29,959
[♪ music increases in tempo]

294
00:20:30,042 --> 00:20:31,794
-[tires screeching]
-[engine revving]

295
00:20:33,045 --> 00:20:34,588
[tires screeching]

296
00:20:34,672 --> 00:20:36,215
[engine accelerating]

297
00:20:38,384 --> 00:20:39,885
-[explosive crash]
-[glass shattering]

298
00:20:42,388 --> 00:20:44,223
-[violent crunching]
-[debris rattling]

299
00:20:49,395 --> 00:20:50,437
[chuckles]

300
00:20:51,105 --> 00:20:53,566
-[engine whirring in reverse]
-[tires screeching]

301
00:20:53,649 --> 00:20:55,150
-[engine revving]
-[tires screeching]

302
00:20:55,609 --> 00:20:57,444
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

303
00:21:04,451 --> 00:21:05,828
[motorcycle approaching]

304
00:21:08,539 --> 00:21:10,165
[♪ music increases in tempo]

305
00:21:10,249 --> 00:21:11,584
[engine idles, shuts off]

306
00:21:19,008 --> 00:21:20,175
[♪ music resumes tempo]

307
00:21:20,926 --> 00:21:22,177
[♪ music increases in tempo]

308
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:40,487
[leaves rustling]

309
00:21:41,447 --> 00:21:42,489
[grunts]

310
00:21:43,449 --> 00:21:44,450
Detective Park.

311
00:21:46,035 --> 00:21:47,328
Detective Choi!

312
00:21:48,162 --> 00:21:50,080
Detective Park, wake up.
[breathing frantically]

313
00:21:51,457 --> 00:21:52,625
[♪ music fades]

314
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,002
EMERGENCY WARD

315
00:21:55,085 --> 00:21:56,337
[monitors beeping steadily]

316
00:21:58,631 --> 00:21:59,632
[hisses in pain]

317
00:22:04,386 --> 00:22:06,305
-[sighs softly]
-[cell phone vibrating]

318
00:22:07,890 --> 00:22:09,058
Hello?

319
00:22:09,141 --> 00:22:11,185
[Byungsik] Yu Seongwon ditched the car
and disappeared.

320
00:22:11,268 --> 00:22:12,728
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

321
00:22:13,479 --> 00:22:15,230
There aren't any cameras here.

322
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:17,441
We'll widen the search area.

323
00:22:19,109 --> 00:22:20,194
[sighs wearily]

324
00:22:23,697 --> 00:22:24,698
[panting] Junyoung.

325
00:22:26,700 --> 00:22:27,701
Jiwon.

326
00:22:28,494 --> 00:22:30,329
How did this happen?

327
00:22:30,412 --> 00:22:31,413
You're badly hurt.

328
00:22:31,497 --> 00:22:34,833
No, I just hurt my neck a little.

329
00:22:35,793 --> 00:22:36,835
[shuddering exhale]

330
00:22:37,753 --> 00:22:38,837
I'm sorry.

331
00:22:40,464 --> 00:22:41,507
It's fine.

332
00:22:42,841 --> 00:22:44,051
I'm just glad you're okay.

333
00:22:44,718 --> 00:22:45,886
[inhales softly]

334
00:22:50,057 --> 00:22:51,225
[Hyera sighs softly]

335
00:22:52,768 --> 00:22:54,228
[Hyera] We're out of options. [sighs]

336
00:22:57,189 --> 00:22:58,691
I'll finish this.

337
00:23:05,447 --> 00:23:06,865
Please look after Isoo.

338
00:23:06,949 --> 00:23:08,575
[♪ music increases in tempo]

339
00:23:15,374 --> 00:23:16,375
[♪ music fades]

340
00:23:16,458 --> 00:23:18,127
JONGHYEON

341
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:19,628
[line ringing]

342
00:23:23,424 --> 00:23:25,467
[automated voice] <i>The number</i>
<i>you have dialed is unavailable...</i>

343
00:23:25,551 --> 00:23:27,011
You can't go in there.

344
00:23:27,094 --> 00:23:29,221
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

345
00:23:33,976 --> 00:23:36,895
Han Jonghyeon was murdered.

346
00:23:36,979 --> 00:23:38,022
[door closes]

347
00:23:45,195 --> 00:23:47,114
Did you order him to kill Yu Seongwon?

348
00:23:49,533 --> 00:23:51,618
What do you mean?
This looks like an accident.

349
00:23:51,702 --> 00:23:54,455
My team was following Han Jonghyeon.

350
00:23:54,538 --> 00:23:57,708
Yu Seongwon killed him and disappeared.

351
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:00,502
So what?

352
00:24:01,795 --> 00:24:03,047
Yu Seongwon will now

353
00:24:04,131 --> 00:24:05,841
come to kill you.

354
00:24:06,842 --> 00:24:07,926
[scoffs]

355
00:24:08,761 --> 00:24:11,638
-Hmm.
-All the evidence is gone,

356
00:24:13,140 --> 00:24:15,476
and he may have considered
leaving like this,

357
00:24:16,268 --> 00:24:18,604
but now that his own mother
tried to kill him,

358
00:24:19,188 --> 00:24:20,272
he won't hold back.

359
00:24:22,232 --> 00:24:25,527
He's been obsessed with dead bodies
and murder since he was a child.

360
00:24:25,611 --> 00:24:26,612
You knew, didn't you?

361
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:30,908
But all you did was
try to hide it and cover it up.

362
00:24:31,950 --> 00:24:33,327
You'll pay the price for that.

363
00:24:34,870 --> 00:24:35,996
If you cooperate with us

364
00:24:38,040 --> 00:24:40,000
and confess to everything that's happened,

365
00:24:40,793 --> 00:24:41,877
we'll protect you.

366
00:24:43,545 --> 00:24:44,546
You will

367
00:24:45,422 --> 00:24:46,840
protect me?

368
00:24:46,924 --> 00:24:47,966
Yes.

369
00:24:48,050 --> 00:24:49,760
If it means we can catch Yu Seongwon.

370
00:24:49,843 --> 00:24:51,303
[scoffs] I don't need it.

371
00:24:52,137 --> 00:24:53,931
I know my son best.

372
00:24:54,014 --> 00:24:55,015
That boy...

373
00:24:57,017 --> 00:24:58,310
can't go against me.

374
00:24:59,603 --> 00:25:01,647
Without me, his life is over, too.

375
00:25:02,731 --> 00:25:04,525
If we don't catch Yu Seongwon now,

376
00:25:05,943 --> 00:25:08,821
you'll have to spend
the rest of your life living in fear.

377
00:25:10,364 --> 00:25:12,199
Never knowing when your son...

378
00:25:13,408 --> 00:25:15,911
might sneak in and kill you.

379
00:25:19,289 --> 00:25:20,541
Are you okay with that?

380
00:25:32,803 --> 00:25:35,973
Then the next time I see you,
I'll be looking at your dead body.

381
00:25:38,517 --> 00:25:40,060
[footsteps receding]

382
00:25:44,773 --> 00:25:46,859
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

383
00:25:58,871 --> 00:26:00,289
[♪ music increases in tempo]

384
00:26:38,827 --> 00:26:39,828
[♪ music fades]

385
00:26:41,663 --> 00:26:43,123
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

386
00:26:43,207 --> 00:26:44,208
Mom.

387
00:26:46,126 --> 00:26:47,377
What are you doing here?

388
00:26:48,962 --> 00:26:50,464
You don't come to my exhibitions.

389
00:26:52,090 --> 00:26:53,258
What?

390
00:26:53,842 --> 00:26:55,594
Are you worried there's evidence here?

391
00:27:00,057 --> 00:27:01,099
[sighs]

392
00:27:01,558 --> 00:27:04,311
Now you're trying
to get rid of my work, too?

393
00:27:04,937 --> 00:27:06,021
[Seongwon] Huh?

394
00:27:07,231 --> 00:27:08,273
[♪ music swells]

395
00:27:11,485 --> 00:27:12,569
[♪ music fades]

396
00:27:15,989 --> 00:27:16,990
Joo Hyera?

397
00:27:21,495 --> 00:27:22,579
[sighs softly]

398
00:27:22,663 --> 00:27:24,373
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

399
00:27:24,456 --> 00:27:27,501
You posed as the victims
to create an alibi, didn't you?

400
00:27:29,002 --> 00:27:30,462
I tried it myself.

401
00:27:31,505 --> 00:27:33,715
How does it feel
to be on the receiving end?

402
00:27:34,508 --> 00:27:35,550
[sighs softly]

403
00:27:37,010 --> 00:27:40,263
Then the next time I see you,
I'll be looking at your dead body.

404
00:27:40,847 --> 00:27:42,140
[footsteps receding]

405
00:27:44,768 --> 00:27:45,769
[Taeseon] Wait.

406
00:27:45,852 --> 00:27:47,813
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

407
00:27:50,774 --> 00:27:52,109
How will you catch him?

408
00:27:54,653 --> 00:27:56,279
I'll pretend to be you.

409
00:27:57,656 --> 00:27:58,657
What?

410
00:27:59,533 --> 00:28:01,576
Are you disappointed I'm not your mom?

411
00:28:02,619 --> 00:28:04,955
No, it's fine.

412
00:28:05,747 --> 00:28:09,209
[exhales softly] I've always wanted
to use you as a model, too.

413
00:28:09,292 --> 00:28:11,044
The detective who was after me

414
00:28:11,128 --> 00:28:14,089
failed to catch me
and became my art in the end.

415
00:28:14,464 --> 00:28:15,507
[chuckles]

416
00:28:18,802 --> 00:28:19,803
Joo Hyera.

417
00:28:23,098 --> 00:28:24,766
How do you want to die?

418
00:28:24,850 --> 00:28:26,018
[♪ music turns ominous]

419
00:28:26,101 --> 00:28:27,144
[scoffs]

420
00:28:28,311 --> 00:28:29,688
How do you want to die?

421
00:28:31,064 --> 00:28:32,274
Today's that day.

422
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:35,318
I was obsessed with you.

423
00:28:35,402 --> 00:28:36,945
I wanted to stop you.

424
00:28:38,113 --> 00:28:39,489
And I wanted to catch you.

425
00:28:40,449 --> 00:28:42,492
But now I'm out of options.

426
00:28:44,745 --> 00:28:46,204
I'll have to kill you.

427
00:28:46,621 --> 00:28:47,748
[scoffs]

428
00:28:48,290 --> 00:28:50,042
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

429
00:28:50,459 --> 00:28:51,877
[grunts, groans]

430
00:28:52,711 --> 00:28:53,795
[groans]

431
00:28:54,337 --> 00:28:55,881
[Seongwon grunting]

432
00:28:57,174 --> 00:28:58,550
-[exhales sharply]
-[grunts]

433
00:28:59,342 --> 00:29:00,385
[groaning]

434
00:29:01,428 --> 00:29:02,721
[dull thud]

435
00:29:03,513 --> 00:29:04,514
Do you get it now?

436
00:29:04,598 --> 00:29:05,724
[groaning]

437
00:29:05,807 --> 00:29:07,726
This is the death you love so much.

438
00:29:07,809 --> 00:29:09,478
[laughing maniacally]

439
00:29:09,561 --> 00:29:10,979
[breathing heavily]

440
00:29:11,063 --> 00:29:13,273
You... [exhales heavily]

441
00:29:13,356 --> 00:29:14,566
...will become a masterpiece.

442
00:29:15,942 --> 00:29:17,069
-[gunshot]
-[squelch]

443
00:29:20,113 --> 00:29:21,239
[distorted thud]

444
00:29:21,323 --> 00:29:23,200
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

445
00:29:26,620 --> 00:29:27,788
[sighs in relief]

446
00:29:31,166 --> 00:29:32,334
[chuckles]

447
00:29:37,422 --> 00:29:38,548
[grunts softly]

448
00:29:46,932 --> 00:29:48,934
[♪ pulsating foreboding music playing]

449
00:29:54,481 --> 00:29:55,482
[exhales sharply]

450
00:30:07,536 --> 00:30:08,578
[exhales sharply]

451
00:30:16,378 --> 00:30:17,546
[♪ music increases in tempo]

452
00:30:18,088 --> 00:30:19,131
[exhales sharply]

453
00:30:25,971 --> 00:30:27,389
[Isoo] Yu Seongwon!

454
00:30:27,472 --> 00:30:29,307
[♪ music resumes tempo]

455
00:30:29,391 --> 00:30:30,392
Isoo!

456
00:30:30,475 --> 00:30:32,477
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

457
00:30:32,561 --> 00:30:33,687
I'm glad you're here.

458
00:30:34,563 --> 00:30:36,314
You need to witness this piece.

459
00:30:38,358 --> 00:30:39,526
You crazy bastard.

460
00:30:42,279 --> 00:30:43,780
It's not finished yet.

461
00:30:44,865 --> 00:30:47,909
Just watch how I turn this woman
into a work of art.

462
00:30:47,993 --> 00:30:50,662
It's the final piece you'll see
before you die.

463
00:30:51,830 --> 00:30:52,831
A work of art?

464
00:30:55,333 --> 00:30:56,501
[♪ music swells]

465
00:31:01,214 --> 00:31:02,382
[shattering]

466
00:31:02,465 --> 00:31:04,217
[♪ gripping, ominous music playing]

467
00:31:05,051 --> 00:31:06,178
Is this a work of art?

468
00:31:10,891 --> 00:31:12,309
[shattering, scattering]

469
00:31:13,310 --> 00:31:14,519
[panting]

470
00:31:16,104 --> 00:31:17,272
This is a work of art?

471
00:31:19,816 --> 00:31:21,276
This is just garbage.

472
00:31:24,821 --> 00:31:27,115
Garbage created by a psychotic killer.

473
00:31:28,992 --> 00:31:30,619
You think you're an artist?

474
00:31:31,703 --> 00:31:33,747
You just want to kill people.

475
00:31:34,789 --> 00:31:37,459
Because you have
this sick obsession with dead bodies.

476
00:31:39,669 --> 00:31:41,963
You dress it up as art

477
00:31:42,047 --> 00:31:44,424
and proudly show it off
for people to see...

478
00:31:47,677 --> 00:31:49,262
but you're just insane.

479
00:31:50,138 --> 00:31:51,389
[sighs heavily]

480
00:31:52,098 --> 00:31:53,600
Do you still not get it?

481
00:31:54,184 --> 00:31:56,728
This is art on a whole other level!

482
00:31:57,646 --> 00:31:58,855
The people I killed

483
00:31:58,939 --> 00:32:01,524
were living meaningless lives.

484
00:32:01,608 --> 00:32:04,903
But I turned them
into something eternally beautiful!

485
00:32:07,656 --> 00:32:08,657
Jo Nayeong.

486
00:32:08,740 --> 00:32:10,825
She couldn't get hired
as a flight attendant,

487
00:32:10,909 --> 00:32:13,411
so she went from
one part-time job to another.

488
00:32:13,495 --> 00:32:16,039
She lived a miserable life
in a basement studio,

489
00:32:16,122 --> 00:32:18,541
but I turned her into something beautiful!

490
00:32:19,793 --> 00:32:21,878
-[Nayeong whimpering softly]
-[Seongwon grunting]

491
00:32:25,006 --> 00:32:27,259
-[whimpering]
-[grunting]

492
00:32:31,513 --> 00:32:32,764
ECSTASY
A BREATHLESS FALL

493
00:32:32,847 --> 00:32:36,017
No one so much as gave her a second look
when she was alive.

494
00:32:36,101 --> 00:32:39,562
But now everyone looks at her
and calls her a beautiful work of art.

495
00:32:41,231 --> 00:32:42,899
Choi Yeongmin.

496
00:32:46,945 --> 00:32:48,613
He had a great body.

497
00:32:49,781 --> 00:32:51,283
So I used a knife.

498
00:32:53,285 --> 00:32:55,745
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

499
00:32:56,496 --> 00:32:57,706
-[squelch]
-[blood splatters]

500
00:32:59,708 --> 00:33:00,875
[♪ ominous sting plays]

501
00:33:00,959 --> 00:33:02,127
[chuckles softly]

502
00:33:04,129 --> 00:33:05,547
[Seongwon] <i>The blood in the air</i>

503
00:33:05,630 --> 00:33:07,340
looked like stars.

504
00:33:07,424 --> 00:33:09,134
CLIMAX
LIGHT SCATTERED ACROSS THE UNIVERSE

505
00:33:12,137 --> 00:33:13,596
And Jeong Minjae.

506
00:33:15,181 --> 00:33:16,975
He blossomed like a flower.

507
00:33:17,058 --> 00:33:18,310
[wet dripping]

508
00:33:34,409 --> 00:33:35,660
[laughs maliciously]

509
00:33:40,665 --> 00:33:43,043
Do you know why people love my work?

510
00:33:44,169 --> 00:33:47,964
They can feel that death is present here
without needing to be told.

511
00:33:48,048 --> 00:33:50,091
Everyone has that urge.

512
00:33:50,633 --> 00:33:51,843
"I want to know death."

513
00:33:52,594 --> 00:33:54,179
"I want to see death."

514
00:33:54,262 --> 00:33:56,056
In the past, they held public executions.

515
00:33:56,139 --> 00:33:59,184
The people watching
would've felt a sense of catharsis.

516
00:33:59,267 --> 00:34:02,020
The exhilaration of being alive
in the face of death.

517
00:34:02,103 --> 00:34:04,064
The desire for true life!

518
00:34:04,147 --> 00:34:05,231
[yelling] That!

519
00:34:05,315 --> 00:34:07,984
That is what I showed them!

520
00:34:08,485 --> 00:34:09,611
[♪ music swells]

521
00:34:13,073 --> 00:34:14,074
[♪ music fades]

522
00:34:14,157 --> 00:34:15,617
I think this is enough.

523
00:34:16,242 --> 00:34:17,410
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

524
00:34:17,494 --> 00:34:18,995
[Hyera] Thanks for the confession.

525
00:34:22,082 --> 00:34:24,709
[♪ dramatic sting plays]

526
00:34:26,419 --> 00:34:27,462
[♪ music fades]

527
00:34:27,545 --> 00:34:28,546
FOUR HOURS EARLIER

528
00:34:28,630 --> 00:34:30,465
We're out of options. [sighs]

529
00:34:30,840 --> 00:34:32,926
-I'll finish this.
-[monitor beeping steadily]

530
00:34:33,009 --> 00:34:34,969
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

531
00:34:38,765 --> 00:34:39,974
Please look after Isoo.

532
00:34:42,185 --> 00:34:43,269
Mmm.

533
00:34:49,984 --> 00:34:51,611
[Isoo, muffled]
What are you planning to do?

534
00:34:52,654 --> 00:34:53,655
[Mr. Choi] Isoo!

535
00:34:57,951 --> 00:34:59,452
-[Hyera] Are you okay?
-[groans softly]

536
00:35:00,328 --> 00:35:01,371
[exhales heavily]

537
00:35:03,581 --> 00:35:06,126
I slept like a log
and now I'm completely refreshed.

538
00:35:06,710 --> 00:35:07,752
[sighs in relief]

539
00:35:08,336 --> 00:35:09,337
So?

540
00:35:10,296 --> 00:35:11,965
How are you going to finish this?

541
00:35:12,048 --> 00:35:13,133
Ah... [sighs]

542
00:35:14,342 --> 00:35:17,220
I'll have to pressure
Jeong Taeseon into confessing.

543
00:35:20,181 --> 00:35:22,183
That won't work on her.

544
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:29,858
Let's set something up.

545
00:35:29,941 --> 00:35:31,901
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

546
00:35:34,070 --> 00:35:35,321
He has a gun?

547
00:35:36,030 --> 00:35:37,157
Yes.

548
00:35:37,240 --> 00:35:39,117
Han Jonghyeon had a gun,

549
00:35:39,701 --> 00:35:40,910
and Yu Seongwon took it.

550
00:35:41,453 --> 00:35:42,871
[panting softly]

551
00:35:46,916 --> 00:35:48,710
Then he'll get even more reckless.

552
00:35:50,628 --> 00:35:51,629
Actually,

553
00:35:53,047 --> 00:35:54,591
that could work to our advantage.

554
00:35:55,383 --> 00:35:56,384
What?

555
00:35:57,510 --> 00:35:59,846
I'll be the bait and lure Yu Seongwon out.

556
00:35:59,929 --> 00:36:00,930
No.

557
00:36:02,348 --> 00:36:03,767
I'll be the bait.

558
00:36:03,850 --> 00:36:05,268
Just explain what the plan is.

559
00:36:05,351 --> 00:36:06,478
[♪ music swells]

560
00:36:08,730 --> 00:36:10,190
-[exhales heavily]
-[♪ music fades]

561
00:36:13,359 --> 00:36:14,569
[vest straps fastening]

562
00:36:14,652 --> 00:36:15,695
[sighs in exasperation]

563
00:36:16,738 --> 00:36:17,947
[Velcro ripping]

564
00:36:18,031 --> 00:36:20,116
I still think it's too dangerous.

565
00:36:20,200 --> 00:36:21,284
Will you be okay?

566
00:36:21,367 --> 00:36:22,452
[Velcro ripping]

567
00:36:22,911 --> 00:36:23,912
[sighs softly]

568
00:36:26,873 --> 00:36:28,583
-I'll make him shoot here.
-[sighs in exasperation]

569
00:36:28,666 --> 00:36:30,084
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

570
00:36:31,753 --> 00:36:33,046
[Velcro ripping]

571
00:36:34,422 --> 00:36:37,300
Isoo. You're still not fully recovered.

572
00:36:37,383 --> 00:36:39,093
I'm really excited right now.

573
00:36:39,177 --> 00:36:42,847
I feel great just thinking
about catching Yu Seongwon. Mmm!

574
00:36:44,057 --> 00:36:45,058
Mr. Choi.

575
00:36:45,683 --> 00:36:46,976
I need to ask you a favor.

576
00:36:47,894 --> 00:36:51,022
Please get the press together
so we can broadcast live.

577
00:36:51,105 --> 00:36:54,359
UBS might try something,
so call all the foreign outlets, too.

578
00:36:54,442 --> 00:36:55,985
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

579
00:36:57,654 --> 00:36:58,780
All right.

580
00:37:00,031 --> 00:37:01,115
I'm off.

581
00:37:07,372 --> 00:37:08,540
[grunts, groans]

582
00:37:09,624 --> 00:37:10,708
[groans]

583
00:37:11,167 --> 00:37:12,377
-[exhales sharply]
-[grunts softly]

584
00:37:13,002 --> 00:37:14,295
[grunts]

585
00:37:14,379 --> 00:37:15,964
You... [breathing heavily]

586
00:37:17,298 --> 00:37:18,508
...will become a masterpiece.

587
00:37:20,093 --> 00:37:21,177
-[gunshot]
-[squelch]

588
00:37:22,178 --> 00:37:25,056
[Isoo] <i>Because you have</i>
<i>this sick obsession with dead bodies.</i>

589
00:37:25,682 --> 00:37:27,392
You dress it up as art

590
00:37:27,475 --> 00:37:30,186
and proudly show it off
for people to see...

591
00:37:31,479 --> 00:37:32,772
but you're just insane.

592
00:37:33,231 --> 00:37:35,692
[sighs heavily] Do you still not get it?

593
00:37:35,775 --> 00:37:38,403
This is art on a whole other level!

594
00:37:39,237 --> 00:37:40,238
The people I killed

595
00:37:40,321 --> 00:37:43,074
were living meaningless lives.

596
00:37:43,157 --> 00:37:46,619
But I turned them
into something eternally beautiful!

597
00:37:47,120 --> 00:37:48,121
Jo Nayeong.

598
00:37:48,204 --> 00:37:50,206
She couldn't get hired
as a flight attendant,

599
00:37:50,290 --> 00:37:53,084
<i>so she went from</i>
<i>one part-time job to another.</i>

600
00:37:53,167 --> 00:37:55,378
<i>She lived a miserable life</i>
<i>in a basement studio,</i>

601
00:37:55,461 --> 00:37:57,005
<i>but I turned her into something beautiful!</i>

602
00:37:57,088 --> 00:38:00,049
Everyone, this is a secret mission,
so please just watch quietly.

603
00:38:00,133 --> 00:38:01,551
-What's the secret mission?
-[reporters murmuring]

604
00:38:01,634 --> 00:38:02,927
[reporter 1] What's going on?

605
00:38:03,011 --> 00:38:06,014
<i>They can feel that death is present here</i>
<i>without needing to be told.</i>

606
00:38:06,097 --> 00:38:08,016
[♪ tense, ominous music playing]

607
00:38:09,267 --> 00:38:10,393
[chuckles]

608
00:38:10,476 --> 00:38:11,728
-[♪ music swells]
-[gunshot]

609
00:38:12,103 --> 00:38:13,479
-[grunts]
-[heavy thud]

610
00:38:13,563 --> 00:38:15,315
[♪ theme music playing]

611
00:38:15,398 --> 00:38:16,733
[panting] Crazy bastard.

612
00:38:19,360 --> 00:38:20,361
Here.

613
00:38:27,285 --> 00:38:28,494
-Yu Seongwon.
-[handcuffs clicking]

614
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:30,455
For the murders of Jo Nayeong...

615
00:38:31,915 --> 00:38:35,501
-[whimpers]
-[Hyera] ...Choi Yeongmin, Kim Heejun,

616
00:38:35,585 --> 00:38:39,047
and Jeong Minjae, you are under arrest.

617
00:38:39,130 --> 00:38:40,340
[breathing heavily]

618
00:38:43,760 --> 00:38:44,886
[murmuring]

619
00:38:54,395 --> 00:38:55,563
There they come.

620
00:38:55,647 --> 00:38:56,648
[reporter 2] He's here!

621
00:38:58,650 --> 00:39:01,069
[reporter 3] Did you confess
to the serial murders?

622
00:39:01,152 --> 00:39:02,987
[reporter 4] When did you
first start killing people?

623
00:39:03,071 --> 00:39:04,364
[clamoring]

624
00:39:06,658 --> 00:39:08,159
You're a pretty big name,

625
00:39:08,993 --> 00:39:11,287
so I called all the foreign press here.

626
00:39:12,080 --> 00:39:13,414
[clamoring continues]

627
00:39:22,966 --> 00:39:24,092
[♪ music fades]

628
00:39:24,175 --> 00:39:25,176
[newscaster 1] <i>This is breaking news.</i>

629
00:39:25,259 --> 00:39:29,305
<i>Sculptor Yu Seongwon's serial murder</i>
<i>confession was broadcast live tonight.</i>

630
00:39:29,389 --> 00:39:32,809
<i>In a shocking revelation, the victims</i>
<i>were the models for his artwork.</i>

631
00:39:32,892 --> 00:39:34,352
[newscaster 2, in English]
<i>This is ANN News.</i>

632
00:39:34,435 --> 00:39:38,356
<i>Seongwon Yu confessed he derived pleasure</i>
<i>from killing his victims.</i>

633
00:39:38,439 --> 00:39:40,316
<i>Prosecutors say he showed no remorse,</i>

634
00:39:40,400 --> 00:39:43,569
<i>even going so far as to belittle</i>
<i>the lives of those he killed.</i>

635
00:39:43,653 --> 00:39:46,447
[newscaster 3] <i>Meanwhile,</i>
<i>police have opened an investigation</i>

636
00:39:46,531 --> 00:39:49,575
<i>after reports suggested</i>
<i>there may have been similar disappearances</i>

637
00:39:49,659 --> 00:39:52,245
<i>during the time Yu was studying</i>
<i>in the United Kingdom.</i>

638
00:39:55,790 --> 00:39:58,292
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

639
00:40:09,303 --> 00:40:10,346
[door closes]

640
00:40:16,060 --> 00:40:17,186
Why aren't you going in?

641
00:40:18,855 --> 00:40:19,939
Ah.

642
00:40:20,440 --> 00:40:21,774
I handed in my resignation.

643
00:40:21,858 --> 00:40:22,859
Your resignation...

644
00:40:23,860 --> 00:40:24,861
has been rejected.

645
00:40:24,944 --> 00:40:26,654
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

646
00:40:31,117 --> 00:40:32,285
Now, go.

647
00:40:33,536 --> 00:40:34,704
Take him down.

648
00:40:36,748 --> 00:40:37,749
Yes, Chief.

649
00:40:41,961 --> 00:40:42,962
[♪ music fades]

650
00:40:44,464 --> 00:40:45,715
[Isoo exhales contentedly]

651
00:40:47,091 --> 00:40:48,843
All right, since you've already confessed,

652
00:40:48,926 --> 00:40:50,803
let's have an honest conversation.

653
00:40:52,096 --> 00:40:53,097
Confessed?

654
00:40:54,474 --> 00:40:57,185
Was that a confession?

655
00:40:58,269 --> 00:41:00,063
What I said earlier

656
00:41:00,146 --> 00:41:03,608
was about the things I'd imagined
while working with those models.

657
00:41:03,691 --> 00:41:04,817
It's not real.

658
00:41:06,152 --> 00:41:07,737
Wait, you actually believed that?

659
00:41:09,572 --> 00:41:11,574
Was my acting that convincing?

660
00:41:13,242 --> 00:41:15,495
Forensics is investigating
your studio right now.

661
00:41:16,579 --> 00:41:18,372
Let's see how you hold out
until we find the evidence.

662
00:41:18,456 --> 00:41:19,457
Evidence?

663
00:41:20,208 --> 00:41:21,250
Will you find any?

664
00:41:22,293 --> 00:41:24,253
Someone seems to have burned it down.

665
00:41:24,337 --> 00:41:26,047
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

666
00:41:39,519 --> 00:41:40,686
[objects clattering]

667
00:41:43,106 --> 00:41:44,649
[♪ music increases in tempo]

668
00:41:49,195 --> 00:41:51,322
[distant clanking]

669
00:41:51,405 --> 00:41:53,074
[camera shutter clicking]

670
00:42:05,211 --> 00:42:06,295
[♪ music swells]

671
00:42:11,551 --> 00:42:12,593
[cell phone vibrates]

672
00:42:13,177 --> 00:42:15,680
Detective Park,
I noticed something strange.

673
00:42:15,763 --> 00:42:16,973
[♪ music fades]

674
00:42:20,434 --> 00:42:21,435
Hey.

675
00:42:22,645 --> 00:42:23,646
By any chance,

676
00:42:24,313 --> 00:42:25,565
are you waiting for you mom?

677
00:42:26,399 --> 00:42:28,192
She's in the next room.

678
00:42:28,276 --> 00:42:30,486
She's here to cooperate
with the investigation

679
00:42:30,570 --> 00:42:32,530
and reveal the entire truth.

680
00:42:32,613 --> 00:42:33,948
[♪ somber, suspenseful music playing]

681
00:42:34,031 --> 00:42:35,783
It's time you stood on your own two feet.

682
00:42:36,617 --> 00:42:38,578
You can't depend on your mom forever.

683
00:42:42,123 --> 00:42:43,249
[Changun] Did you know

684
00:42:44,375 --> 00:42:47,420
the person who hired Cho Pilgu...
[inhales sharply]

685
00:42:50,923 --> 00:42:53,092
...to kill Kim Younghwan was Yu Seongwon?

686
00:42:54,802 --> 00:42:56,846
Are you saying
you gave the order to kill him?

687
00:42:56,929 --> 00:42:57,972
Yes.

688
00:42:58,055 --> 00:42:59,182
Why?

689
00:43:00,057 --> 00:43:02,143
Just because. I thought it'd be fun.

690
00:43:03,811 --> 00:43:05,021
No.

691
00:43:05,104 --> 00:43:08,316
You knew, and that's why you ordered
your secretary, Han Jonghyeon,

692
00:43:08,399 --> 00:43:11,485
to kill Cho Pilgu while he was in custody.
Isn't that right?

693
00:43:12,570 --> 00:43:13,571
I...

694
00:43:15,364 --> 00:43:16,657
didn't know anything.

695
00:43:17,491 --> 00:43:18,534
I'm telling the truth.

696
00:43:28,544 --> 00:43:30,046
Well done.

697
00:43:30,129 --> 00:43:31,839
[Changun] You didn't know anything?

698
00:43:33,674 --> 00:43:37,386
Didn't Detective Joo Hyera
make it clear to you?

699
00:43:39,263 --> 00:43:40,306
Your son is a murderer.

700
00:43:42,475 --> 00:43:44,101
He killed five people.

701
00:43:45,728 --> 00:43:47,146
[Taeseon] You know, don't you?

702
00:43:47,230 --> 00:43:48,731
I thought she had it wrong.

703
00:43:48,814 --> 00:43:50,274
I never imagined

704
00:43:50,358 --> 00:43:53,986
that my son could've done
something like that.

705
00:43:54,070 --> 00:43:57,365
Then why did Han Jonghyeon kill Cho Pilgu?

706
00:43:58,074 --> 00:44:00,910
Maybe Seongwon asked him to do it.

707
00:44:00,993 --> 00:44:03,246
They were close, like brothers.

708
00:44:20,554 --> 00:44:21,639
[♪ music fades]

709
00:44:21,722 --> 00:44:24,433
Chairwoman Jeong is still denying
she knows anything.

710
00:44:25,017 --> 00:44:28,354
She claims Yu Seongwon must have
put Han Jonghyeon up to it.

711
00:44:31,232 --> 00:44:32,233
What about Yu Seongwon?

712
00:44:33,567 --> 00:44:35,653
He keeps insisting it wasn't a confession.

713
00:44:36,445 --> 00:44:37,530
[sighs softly]

714
00:44:37,613 --> 00:44:39,365
What about Han Jonghyeon's phone?

715
00:44:39,949 --> 00:44:42,743
There's a record of him calling
the chairwoman, but no recording.

716
00:44:43,327 --> 00:44:44,787
Ah, so... [inhales sharply]

717
00:44:45,454 --> 00:44:48,666
I do have a recording,
but it's from a bug, so we can't use it.

718
00:44:48,749 --> 00:44:49,917
You planted a bug?

719
00:44:50,626 --> 00:44:51,752
Yes.

720
00:44:55,840 --> 00:44:57,300
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

721
00:44:57,383 --> 00:44:58,884
[Taeseon] <i>To cover all this up,</i>

722
00:44:59,760 --> 00:45:02,054
<i>I think Seongwon</i>
<i>will have to commit suicide.</i>

723
00:45:03,306 --> 00:45:05,516
<i>A mentally unstable artist</i>

724
00:45:05,599 --> 00:45:07,601
<i>takes his life</i>
<i>after his studio burns down.</i>

725
00:45:08,352 --> 00:45:10,396
The murder cases are closed unsolved.

726
00:45:15,109 --> 00:45:16,736
And I'll become a poor mother

727
00:45:18,654 --> 00:45:20,906
who lost her child.

728
00:45:22,783 --> 00:45:24,201
[exhales incredulously]

729
00:45:24,910 --> 00:45:27,079
She told him to kill her own son.

730
00:45:28,581 --> 00:45:30,833
That's why Yu Seongwon killed
Han Jonghyeon.

731
00:45:32,460 --> 00:45:35,588
Detective Park and Detective Choi
witnessed that, so we can prove that.

732
00:45:35,671 --> 00:45:36,756
No.

733
00:45:36,839 --> 00:45:39,550
Han Jonghyeon had a gun,

734
00:45:39,633 --> 00:45:41,177
so he'll just claim self-defense.

735
00:45:42,678 --> 00:45:44,805
If we want to prove his serial murders...

736
00:45:44,889 --> 00:45:46,557
We need something from the studio.

737
00:45:48,934 --> 00:45:51,479
We need to unmask that woman, too.

738
00:45:54,190 --> 00:45:56,484
You should talk to the police chief.

739
00:45:57,193 --> 00:46:00,029
I can't go into detail
because I made a promise,

740
00:46:00,696 --> 00:46:02,114
but I think they know each other.

741
00:46:05,534 --> 00:46:06,577
[♪ music fades]

742
00:46:07,828 --> 00:46:08,829
[door opens]

743
00:46:09,789 --> 00:46:11,415
[Taegyun] What?

744
00:46:11,499 --> 00:46:12,625
What is it?

745
00:46:14,835 --> 00:46:17,671
Chairwoman Jeong Taeseon
mentioned you, sir.

746
00:46:19,507 --> 00:46:20,508
How did this happen?

747
00:46:21,967 --> 00:46:24,804
I only told her we had a suspect.

748
00:46:25,429 --> 00:46:27,598
That's all I told her. About Hwang Jongsu.

749
00:46:27,681 --> 00:46:30,017
-How could you tell her that?
-[nervously] Uh...

750
00:46:30,101 --> 00:46:32,019
I really didn't know!

751
00:46:32,103 --> 00:46:36,023
How could I have known
that Yu Seongwon really was a killer?

752
00:46:36,107 --> 00:46:38,692
Chief Park, what do I do?

753
00:46:38,776 --> 00:46:40,486
What do I do?

754
00:46:40,569 --> 00:46:42,363
What am I going to do?

755
00:46:42,446 --> 00:46:43,781
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

756
00:46:55,418 --> 00:46:58,796
What happened with the Hwang Jongsu case?

757
00:46:59,713 --> 00:47:00,840
Hwang Jongsu?

758
00:47:02,550 --> 00:47:04,635
How is that a case? He committed suicide.

759
00:47:04,718 --> 00:47:05,719
[bangs table]

760
00:47:06,303 --> 00:47:07,972
Inducing suicide is a crime, too.

761
00:47:10,057 --> 00:47:12,017
I know the police chief
gave you information

762
00:47:12,101 --> 00:47:13,602
about our suspect, Hwang Jongsu.

763
00:47:14,603 --> 00:47:17,648
Did you send reporters there
to put pressure on Detective Jin,

764
00:47:18,357 --> 00:47:19,692
then tell Hwang to commit suicide?

765
00:47:19,775 --> 00:47:21,402
What are you talking about?

766
00:47:23,028 --> 00:47:26,365
He asked me to send our news team
because detectives were chasing him.

767
00:47:26,449 --> 00:47:30,119
He said he wanted to go on camera
and declare his innocence.

768
00:47:31,745 --> 00:47:33,330
Mr. Hwang probably died

769
00:47:33,414 --> 00:47:35,249
because of Jin Isoo.

770
00:47:35,332 --> 00:47:37,126
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

771
00:47:37,209 --> 00:47:38,669
Maybe he pushed him from behind.

772
00:47:43,174 --> 00:47:44,300
Over here.

773
00:47:46,135 --> 00:47:47,803
[police dogs panting]

774
00:47:49,555 --> 00:47:51,182
[♪ music increases in tempo]

775
00:47:51,849 --> 00:47:53,017
[sniffing eagerly]

776
00:47:56,896 --> 00:47:58,772
[police dogs panting, sniffing]

777
00:48:02,776 --> 00:48:04,695
[barking]

778
00:48:08,365 --> 00:48:10,117
[both barking]

779
00:48:10,201 --> 00:48:12,536
[♪ music swells, fades]

780
00:48:12,620 --> 00:48:16,248
Your mom seems determined
to pin everything on you.

781
00:48:16,332 --> 00:48:18,876
She says you ordered
the murder of Cho Pilgu.

782
00:48:18,959 --> 00:48:20,377
She says she knows nothing.

783
00:48:20,461 --> 00:48:22,046
Who's Cho Pilgu?

784
00:48:22,129 --> 00:48:23,672
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

785
00:48:23,756 --> 00:48:27,676
Can you prove a single thing
you've been saying?

786
00:48:28,886 --> 00:48:30,596
All the people you claim I killed

787
00:48:30,679 --> 00:48:32,515
were still alive after they met me.

788
00:48:32,598 --> 00:48:36,101
The murder display in my studio?

789
00:48:36,185 --> 00:48:37,186
It burned down.

790
00:48:38,145 --> 00:48:40,022
Cho Pilgu, who killed Kim Younghwan,

791
00:48:40,105 --> 00:48:41,857
Han Jonghyeon, who killed Cho Pilgu,

792
00:48:41,941 --> 00:48:43,984
and even Mr. Hwang,
the suspect you were chasing,

793
00:48:44,068 --> 00:48:45,361
are all dead.

794
00:48:45,444 --> 00:48:47,238
[♪ suspenseful, pulsating music playing]

795
00:48:47,321 --> 00:48:48,948
You failed.

796
00:48:50,574 --> 00:48:51,742
Just admit it.

797
00:48:52,743 --> 00:48:54,328
[cell phone vibrating]

798
00:48:54,411 --> 00:48:57,081
DETECTIVE PARK JUNYOUNG

799
00:48:57,164 --> 00:48:58,207
[♪ music swells]

800
00:49:01,544 --> 00:49:02,753
[Junyoung] <i>We found them.</i>

801
00:49:03,587 --> 00:49:06,423
Three bodies were buried in his yard.

802
00:49:14,056 --> 00:49:15,516
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

803
00:49:16,850 --> 00:49:18,394
We found the bodies in your yard.

804
00:49:21,855 --> 00:49:23,732
You buried the bodies in your yard,

805
00:49:24,817 --> 00:49:26,151
walked over them,

806
00:49:27,111 --> 00:49:28,112
and drank tea,

807
00:49:32,783 --> 00:49:34,910
making them look up to you even in death.

808
00:49:36,370 --> 00:49:37,371
You're right.

809
00:49:39,415 --> 00:49:40,791
Because they're mine.

810
00:49:46,755 --> 00:49:48,173
They're mine.

811
00:49:53,804 --> 00:49:55,806
Mine.

812
00:49:56,890 --> 00:50:01,061
Even their bodies rotting inside the earth

813
00:50:01,145 --> 00:50:03,105
are all mine.

814
00:50:03,564 --> 00:50:05,816
-[bangs table]
-[angrily] They're my art!

815
00:50:05,899 --> 00:50:07,651
[shuddering breath of rage]

816
00:50:09,528 --> 00:50:10,738
So this is your ending.

817
00:50:14,617 --> 00:50:17,411
A murderer who pretended to be an artist.

818
00:50:18,203 --> 00:50:19,455
No.

819
00:50:20,289 --> 00:50:23,167
My name, my art

820
00:50:23,792 --> 00:50:25,210
will become even more famous.

821
00:50:26,420 --> 00:50:28,047
[yelling] The whole world

822
00:50:28,130 --> 00:50:30,633
will remember me forever.

823
00:50:31,133 --> 00:50:32,760
[shuddering breath of rage]

824
00:50:35,346 --> 00:50:36,347
You're right.

825
00:50:36,847 --> 00:50:38,098
[in a low voice] Ah...

826
00:50:38,932 --> 00:50:40,643
-[Isoo] That's true.
-[chuckling]

827
00:50:43,812 --> 00:50:44,813
But you

828
00:50:45,689 --> 00:50:46,899
won't get to see that.

829
00:50:47,566 --> 00:50:48,692
You'll be behind bars.

830
00:50:50,235 --> 00:50:51,654
Actually, instead of prison,

831
00:50:52,529 --> 00:50:54,657
you might end up
in a psychiatric hospital.

832
00:50:54,740 --> 00:50:56,700
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

833
00:51:00,704 --> 00:51:01,705
What a shame.

834
00:51:02,831 --> 00:51:04,875
You hate being locked up
in a hospital room.

835
00:51:06,418 --> 00:51:08,170
Dr. Seo told me everything.

836
00:51:10,506 --> 00:51:12,549
Looks like you'll be wearing
a straitjacket again.

837
00:51:14,635 --> 00:51:15,636
[chuckles softly]

838
00:51:15,719 --> 00:51:16,720
Have fun.

839
00:51:18,931 --> 00:51:20,265
[Seongwon's breath trembling]

840
00:51:23,227 --> 00:51:25,312
[screaming]

841
00:51:28,190 --> 00:51:30,109
[♪ somber, ominous music playing]

842
00:51:31,485 --> 00:51:33,028
[breathing raggedly]

843
00:51:34,196 --> 00:51:35,280
[gasping sharply]

844
00:51:39,201 --> 00:51:41,245
[whimpering brokenly]

845
00:51:46,375 --> 00:51:48,836
[screaming hysterically]

846
00:51:59,596 --> 00:52:00,723
[♪ music fades]

847
00:52:00,806 --> 00:52:02,558
I think I've cooperated enough.

848
00:52:03,642 --> 00:52:05,519
-Need I do more?
-Let's stop here.

849
00:52:18,907 --> 00:52:19,950
[sighs wearily]

850
00:52:23,078 --> 00:52:24,079
Chairwoman.

851
00:52:25,622 --> 00:52:26,623
Where are you going?

852
00:52:29,209 --> 00:52:30,335
Ms. Jeong Taeseon.

853
00:52:30,419 --> 00:52:35,132
You are under arrest for soliciting
the murder of Cho Pilgu and Yu Seongwon.

854
00:52:35,215 --> 00:52:37,259
What are you doing? Do you have proof?

855
00:52:38,010 --> 00:52:41,930
I played this for your son,
and he hit the roof.

856
00:52:43,640 --> 00:52:45,350
[Taeseon] <i>To cover all this up,</i>

857
00:52:46,560 --> 00:52:48,812
<i>I think Seongwon</i>
<i>will have to commit suicide.</i>

858
00:52:49,730 --> 00:52:51,899
<i>A mentally unstable artist</i>

859
00:52:51,982 --> 00:52:53,901
<i>takes his life</i>
<i>after his studio burns down.</i>

860
00:52:55,569 --> 00:52:56,779
[scoffs sarcastically]

861
00:52:56,862 --> 00:52:57,863
[breathes deeply]

862
00:52:57,946 --> 00:52:59,656
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

863
00:52:59,740 --> 00:53:01,200
You bugged my office?

864
00:53:01,283 --> 00:53:02,534
Yes.

865
00:53:02,618 --> 00:53:04,536
See? What did I tell you?

866
00:53:04,620 --> 00:53:07,539
You should've come here
wearing the 18-karat bracelet I gave you.

867
00:53:08,207 --> 00:53:09,416
Just look at the mess you're in.

868
00:53:09,500 --> 00:53:10,667
It breaks my heart.

869
00:53:11,376 --> 00:53:14,379
Go inside and talk to our handsome chief.
Go back inside.

870
00:53:14,463 --> 00:53:15,923
-Jin Isoo.
-Hurry back inside.

871
00:53:16,006 --> 00:53:19,676
Jin Isoo. I'll make you pay for this!

872
00:53:19,760 --> 00:53:21,261
I'll make you pay!

873
00:53:21,345 --> 00:53:22,554
Oh, I'm not scared at all.

874
00:53:23,138 --> 00:53:24,306
[chuckles]

875
00:53:25,432 --> 00:53:26,600
[door closes]

876
00:53:28,393 --> 00:53:29,394
SHOCKING ARREST OF MOTHER AND SON

877
00:53:29,478 --> 00:53:30,813
A CONFESSION THAT SHOCKED THE WORLD

878
00:53:30,896 --> 00:53:32,064
[camera shutter clicking]

879
00:53:32,147 --> 00:53:33,440
POLICE CHIEF FACES DISCIPLINARY HEARING

880
00:53:33,524 --> 00:53:35,317
MOTHER SOLICITS MURDER TO PROTECT HER SON

881
00:53:35,400 --> 00:53:36,860
JIN ISOO HOLDS JOINT FUNERAL FOR VICTIMS

882
00:53:36,944 --> 00:53:38,904
MAY THEY REST IN PEACE

883
00:53:38,987 --> 00:53:41,073
HANSU GROUP,
GANGHA POLICE STATION, JOO HYERA

884
00:53:41,156 --> 00:53:43,492
OUR DEEPEST CONDOLENCES
MAY THEY REST IN PEACE

885
00:53:43,575 --> 00:53:45,994
CHOI YEONGMIN, KIM HEEJUN, JO NAYEONG

886
00:53:46,078 --> 00:53:48,038
[♪ somber, melancholy music playing]

887
00:53:48,121 --> 00:53:49,581
Let us have a moment of silence.

888
00:53:50,791 --> 00:53:52,125
[woman sobbing]

889
00:53:52,209 --> 00:53:53,669
[scattered sobbing]

890
00:53:58,507 --> 00:53:59,508
Thank you.

891
00:54:01,260 --> 00:54:03,220
[scattered sobbing, sniffling]

892
00:54:07,933 --> 00:54:09,268
[woman sobbing bitterly]

893
00:54:11,687 --> 00:54:13,522
[scattered sobbing, sniffling continues]

894
00:54:13,605 --> 00:54:16,108
[woman] I can't bear
to let you go like this.

895
00:54:16,191 --> 00:54:17,860
How can I let you go?

896
00:54:23,574 --> 00:54:25,242
[woman continues sobbing bitterly]

897
00:54:36,545 --> 00:54:37,921
Thank you.

898
00:54:47,806 --> 00:54:49,224
[breath trembles, sniffles]

899
00:55:04,156 --> 00:55:06,366
[♪ somber, melancholy music continues]

900
00:55:35,729 --> 00:55:36,772
[♪ music fades]

901
00:55:39,524 --> 00:55:42,653
I suddenly couldn't breathe
and my body just froze.

902
00:55:42,736 --> 00:55:44,696
I couldn't even trust myself.

903
00:55:44,780 --> 00:55:48,241
I even wondered
if I should quit being a cop.

904
00:55:49,493 --> 00:55:51,078
But after I caught Yu Seongwon,

905
00:55:51,745 --> 00:55:54,998
I've been sleeping well,
and I feel more at ease.

906
00:55:56,124 --> 00:55:58,502
I somehow feel like
I can get through this.

907
00:55:58,585 --> 00:55:59,586
I'm glad to hear that.

908
00:56:00,295 --> 00:56:02,923
I think doing meaningful work
is helping you get better.

909
00:56:03,006 --> 00:56:04,383
Exactly.

910
00:56:04,466 --> 00:56:07,135
Thank goodness I became a detective.

911
00:56:08,011 --> 00:56:11,515
Investigating is so much fun,
catching bad guys is so rewarding,

912
00:56:11,890 --> 00:56:13,892
and my teammates... [chuckles softly]

913
00:56:14,393 --> 00:56:16,853
They're clueless, but they're good people.

914
00:56:17,771 --> 00:56:19,773
Would you like to see? Here.

915
00:56:19,856 --> 00:56:20,941
[♪ jaunty music playing]

916
00:56:21,024 --> 00:56:23,485
This tall, feeble-looking one
is Detective Joo.

917
00:56:23,568 --> 00:56:24,611
-Okay.
-The right, tall one.

918
00:56:24,695 --> 00:56:26,405
He has a girlfriend now. He's Junyoung.

919
00:56:26,488 --> 00:56:28,448
The curly hair is our youngest teammate.

920
00:56:28,532 --> 00:56:30,367
He claims he has a girlfriend.

921
00:56:30,450 --> 00:56:32,035
And this good-looking man here.

922
00:56:32,119 --> 00:56:34,413
That's me. This is
Violent Crime Investigation Team 1.

923
00:56:34,496 --> 00:56:35,997
-I see.
-Amazing, right?

924
00:56:36,748 --> 00:56:38,041
Gangha Police Violent Crime Team 1,

925
00:56:38,125 --> 00:56:39,918
in investigating a serial murder case

926
00:56:40,001 --> 00:56:43,255
whose perpetrator had long evaded
capture through sophisticated methods,

927
00:56:43,338 --> 00:56:47,217
apprehended the suspect with outstanding
investigative skill and determination,

928
00:56:47,300 --> 00:56:50,804
and demonstrated exemplary dedication
and devotion to duty as police officers,

929
00:56:50,887 --> 00:56:52,514
and is hereby commended.

930
00:56:52,597 --> 00:56:56,143
Gangha Police Violent Crime Team 1,
Senior Inspector Joo Hyera.

931
00:56:56,226 --> 00:56:57,436
[all applauding]

932
00:56:59,688 --> 00:57:00,689
What's wrong with you?

933
00:57:00,772 --> 00:57:03,859
[announcer] Gangha Police Violent Crime
Team 1, Senior Inspector Jin Isoo.

934
00:57:03,942 --> 00:57:05,652
[all applauding]

935
00:57:10,365 --> 00:57:11,366
[loudly] Thank you, sir!

936
00:57:11,450 --> 00:57:12,909
[laughing]

937
00:57:12,993 --> 00:57:14,911
[announcer] Inspector Park Junyoung.

938
00:57:14,995 --> 00:57:17,581
[squeals] You're so handsome,
Park Junyoung!

939
00:57:17,664 --> 00:57:19,166
[all applauding]

940
00:57:19,916 --> 00:57:21,001
[loudly] Thank you, sir!

941
00:57:22,419 --> 00:57:24,087
[announcer] Senior Police Officer
Choi Kyungjin.

942
00:57:24,171 --> 00:57:25,464
[all applauding]

943
00:57:25,547 --> 00:57:26,548
[loudly] Thank you, sir!

944
00:57:27,299 --> 00:57:29,176
Hurry up and get in here. Ready?

945
00:57:29,259 --> 00:57:31,136
-One, two, three!
-[camera shutter clicks]

946
00:57:31,219 --> 00:57:32,220
Perfect.

947
00:57:33,555 --> 00:57:34,556
Huh?

948
00:57:34,639 --> 00:57:37,601
Mr. Choi, I think
you're late for your flight.

949
00:57:38,143 --> 00:57:39,144
I'm not late.

950
00:57:39,728 --> 00:57:41,563
Ah! You're late. Let's take my car.

951
00:57:41,646 --> 00:57:43,190
-[Mr. Choi] I'm fine.
-Let's go. We're off.

952
00:57:43,273 --> 00:57:45,108
-Sorry, goodbye.
-No problem. Goodbye.

953
00:57:45,776 --> 00:57:46,777
[♪ music fades]

954
00:57:46,860 --> 00:57:48,111
[engine purring smoothly]

955
00:57:55,160 --> 00:57:57,329
Are you really going to go like that?

956
00:57:58,747 --> 00:58:01,708
Why would you wear
a suit on a trip to Europe?

957
00:58:01,792 --> 00:58:03,627
I told you, I'm comfortable in this.

958
00:58:03,710 --> 00:58:05,962
But it's a long-haul flight.

959
00:58:07,297 --> 00:58:09,800
-[sighs in exasperation] I give up.
-[chuckles]

960
00:58:09,883 --> 00:58:11,259
[♪ gentle, tender music playing]

961
00:58:11,343 --> 00:58:14,471
Have fun, get plenty of rest,
and take your full vacation.

962
00:58:15,055 --> 00:58:17,182
All right. Thank you.

963
00:58:18,183 --> 00:58:19,434
Did you pack your meds?

964
00:58:19,518 --> 00:58:20,894
If anything happens--

965
00:58:20,977 --> 00:58:23,188
Ah, all right, now stop.

966
00:58:23,271 --> 00:58:26,650
[sighs] I'm worried.
Maybe I should go with you.

967
00:58:26,733 --> 00:58:29,110
I heard your team is
going on vacation as a reward.

968
00:58:29,194 --> 00:58:30,987
We can change the destination to Europe.

969
00:58:31,071 --> 00:58:32,656
I must decline.

970
00:58:33,865 --> 00:58:35,033
[chuckles softly]

971
00:58:38,453 --> 00:58:39,621
[both chuckle]

972
00:58:40,413 --> 00:58:41,456
[♪ music fades]

973
00:58:46,628 --> 00:58:48,046
Have a great trip.

974
00:58:49,005 --> 00:58:50,757
All right. Take care.

975
00:58:51,675 --> 00:58:54,261
I don't feel good sending you off so far.

976
00:58:55,220 --> 00:58:56,221
How about a hug?

977
00:58:56,805 --> 00:58:57,806
[chuckles]

978
00:58:57,889 --> 00:58:59,307
[♪ gentle, tender music playing]

979
00:58:59,391 --> 00:59:00,392
[chuckles softly]

980
00:59:00,767 --> 00:59:01,935
[Isoo exhales contentedly]

981
00:59:03,103 --> 00:59:04,104
Mmm.

982
00:59:10,026 --> 00:59:11,027
I'll be back soon.

983
00:59:12,237 --> 00:59:13,238
Go on inside.

984
00:59:13,321 --> 00:59:14,322
[chuckles softly]

985
00:59:24,082 --> 00:59:25,083
[sighs contentedly]

986
00:59:29,796 --> 00:59:30,881
Mr. Choi Jeonghun.

987
00:59:32,048 --> 00:59:33,925
Oh! [chortles]

988
00:59:34,009 --> 00:59:35,385
Hello.

989
00:59:35,468 --> 00:59:37,345
Where are you going? A business trip?

990
00:59:37,429 --> 00:59:38,471
No.

991
00:59:39,306 --> 00:59:40,390
I'm going on vacation.

992
00:59:40,473 --> 00:59:41,516
Finally.

993
00:59:41,600 --> 00:59:43,643
-Wow.
-[both chuckle]

994
00:59:43,727 --> 00:59:45,103
I'm leaving today, too.

995
00:59:45,729 --> 00:59:47,314
-Really?
-Where are you headed?

996
00:59:48,148 --> 00:59:49,399
I'm going to...

997
00:59:49,482 --> 00:59:50,734
[♪ music increases in tempo]

998
01:00:00,368 --> 01:00:01,369
Me too.

999
01:00:03,830 --> 01:00:04,956
[chuckles]

1000
01:00:05,040 --> 01:00:06,207
[chuckles softly]

1001
01:00:09,044 --> 01:00:10,170
[♪ music fades]

1002
01:00:10,253 --> 01:00:12,005
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

1003
01:00:16,051 --> 01:00:17,218
[exhales contentedly]

1004
01:00:22,307 --> 01:00:24,935
Bro. I thought we were going abroad.

1005
01:00:25,018 --> 01:00:26,728
We can't just take off as Korean cops.

1006
01:00:26,811 --> 01:00:28,688
We have a country to protect.

1007
01:00:28,772 --> 01:00:30,023
Having said that,

1008
01:00:30,732 --> 01:00:32,442
this is our reward vacation.

1009
01:00:33,068 --> 01:00:34,778
Yeah. [exhales contentedly]

1010
01:00:34,861 --> 01:00:38,031
I can't remember the last time
I had a break like this.

1011
01:00:38,114 --> 01:00:39,324
[sighs contentedly]

1012
01:00:40,325 --> 01:00:41,326
What's taking so long?

1013
01:00:41,409 --> 01:00:43,495
Women always take forever.

1014
01:00:43,578 --> 01:00:46,706
Oh. What are they even doing in there?
[scoffs]

1015
01:00:59,719 --> 01:01:00,762
Are you going for a dive?

1016
01:01:00,845 --> 01:01:02,138
Whatever.

1017
01:01:02,222 --> 01:01:04,975
-Is this good?
-What's with the whistle?

1018
01:01:05,934 --> 01:01:07,102
Aren't we going out there?

1019
01:01:09,896 --> 01:01:11,523
Right, we should.

1020
01:01:12,190 --> 01:01:13,817
-Let's go!
-Move out!

1021
01:01:13,900 --> 01:01:15,068
-[Kyungjin] Let's go!
-[Isoo] Let's go!

1022
01:01:17,862 --> 01:01:19,072
REWARD VACATION!!
JIN ISOO'S TREAT!

1023
01:01:19,155 --> 01:01:20,657
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1024
01:01:20,740 --> 01:01:22,158
-Whoo!
-[screaming]

1025
01:02:11,624 --> 01:02:12,709
[♪ music fades]

1026
01:02:15,587 --> 01:02:17,547
[♪ suspenseful, ominous music playing]

1027
01:02:41,821 --> 01:02:43,406
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1028
01:02:45,575 --> 01:02:46,743
[♪ music swells]

1029
01:03:06,471 --> 01:03:07,722
[exhales heavily]

1030
01:03:13,728 --> 01:03:14,813
[♪ music fades]

1031
01:03:19,818 --> 01:03:20,819
[exhales softly]

1032
01:03:20,902 --> 01:03:22,821
Jin Isoo, get changed.

1033
01:03:23,530 --> 01:03:24,531
Why?

1034
01:03:25,073 --> 01:03:26,199
[sighs] We have a case.

1035
01:03:27,992 --> 01:03:28,993
A case?

1036
01:03:31,037 --> 01:03:32,288
Looks like we've got ourselves...

1037
01:03:32,372 --> 01:03:34,124
A most interesting case, right?

1038
01:03:36,876 --> 01:03:38,336
Let's go, Detective Joo.

1039
01:03:38,419 --> 01:03:40,171
[microphone feedback]

1040
01:03:42,173 --> 01:03:43,174
We have a case.

1041
01:03:43,842 --> 01:03:44,843
Let's go.

1042
01:03:44,926 --> 01:03:47,137
[♪ theme music playing]

1043
01:04:17,500 --> 01:04:18,501
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 14

1044
01:04:18,585 --> 01:04:19,961
VIOLENT CRIME TEAM 1
OFF TO THE NEXT CASE!

1045
01:04:41,065 --> 01:04:44,485
Special Cast. Yoo Seungho

1046
01:04:44,569 --> 01:04:47,989
Special Cast. Kim Hyeeun

1047
01:04:48,072 --> 01:04:51,492
Special Cast. Kim Jihun

1048
01:04:58,291 --> 01:05:00,084
JIN ISOO
AHN BOHYUN

1049
01:05:03,296 --> 01:05:05,089
JOO HYERA
JUNG EUNCHAE

1050
01:05:07,175 --> 01:05:09,093
PARK JUNYOUNG
KANG SANGJUN

1051
01:05:11,221 --> 01:05:13,097
CHOI KYUNGJIN
KIM SHINBI

1052
01:05:15,225 --> 01:05:17,060
YOON JIWON
JUNG GAHEE

1053
